{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured a persistent HTTP forward proxy on node1:3128. Node2 can retrieve only its approved handbook origin on node2:8081; wrong ports, wrong destinations, and all CONNECT tunnels return HTTP 403. Both nodes passed sequential restart and recovery verification.","actions_performed":["Installed the supported RHEL AppStream Squid 6.10 package on node1.","Applied a minimal Squid ACL policy and retained the packaged configuration as /etc/squid/squid.conf.rpm-baseline.","Created a hardened, enabled systemd service for the preserved staged origin on node2.","Added persistent, source-scoped firewalld rules for node2→node1:3128 and node1→node2:8081.","Verified allowed and denied behavior before and after restarting each node sequentially.","Confirmed SELinux remains enforcing, SSH remains active, no failed units exist, and no temporary residue remains."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Proxy, destination policy, and complete client behavior","command_ids":["cmd-416b46b0ec334153","cmd-69f2698318c44f20","cmd-29aef1dfd4974cfe","cmd-62a97492fce4499d"],"summary":"Squid configuration permits node2 only to node2:8081, denies CONNECT first, and denies everything else. Tests returned the exact handbook content while wrong port, wrong host, and CONNECT returned 403; Squid logs corroborate every decision."},{"requirement":"Persistent origin and narrowly scoped network exposure","command_ids":["cmd-34b1873fbf864c66","cmd-de3e3f11f9254f68","cmd-5371381410ae44b9","cmd-05931820c1e44489"],"summary":"The enabled hardened origin service recovered on port 8081, and persistent firewalld rules expose each service only to its required peer."},{"requirement":"Preserve the staged origin application","command_ids":["cmd-1dec976f5ccb476f","cmd-29aef1dfd4974cfe","cmd-05931820c1e44489"],"summary":"Pre-change and final SHA-256 values match for handbook.txt and serve.py."},{"requirement":"Preserve operating-system release and kernel","command_ids":["cmd-906baec30d254817","